            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> The Py_mod_create docs say it should return a new module object \n\nThat implies that the newref path is always wrong even without module state and mostly works by luck.\n\nIt's a bit of a shame that it has to fail completely. One of the nice things about (the idea of) module state is that it probably should be possible for it to import it multiple times. I think with the current lookup code that certainly isn't possible.",
